---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const org = "https://github.com/ternmesh";
---

<Base
    title="Apps"
    description="Tern's apps for Android, for iPhone, iPad and Mac, and in the browser: what each runs on and where to get it."
>
    <section class="apps wrap">
        <h1>The apps</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            An app is how you use a Tern node: it talks to the node over Bluetooth or USB, and the node does the
            radio. Every one of them needs a node with Tern's firmware, which you can
            <a href="/flash">put on a Heltec V3</a> from a browser.
        </p>
        <p class="note">
            This is an alpha of a draft protocol. Its cryptography has not been reviewed: do not trust it with
            anything that matters.
        </p>

        <ul class="list">
            <li class="card" id="android">
                <h2>Android</h2>
                <p class="muted">Android 8 or later.</p>
                <p>
                    Chats with contacts and groups, adding a contact by its QR code or link, sharing your position on
                    a map with the people you choose, the node's battery and settings, and updates to its firmware
                    over Bluetooth. A node's link opens in the app.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <a class="button" href={`${org}/android/releases/latest`}>Download the APK</a>
                </p>
                <p class="muted small">
                    From the app's latest release on GitHub. Open the file on the phone; Android asks first to be
                    allowed to install apps from your browser. The APK is signed with the project's release key, so a
                    newer one installs over an older one. Source and issues:
                    <a href={`${org}/android`}>ternmesh/android</a>.
                </p>
            </li>

            <li class="card" id="apple">
                <h2>iPhone, iPad and Mac</h2>
                <p class="muted">iOS 16 or later, macOS 13 or later.</p>
                <p>
                    One app for all three: chats with contacts and groups, adding a contact by its QR code on iPhone
                    and iPad or its link anywhere, sharing your position on a map, the node's battery and settings,
                    and updates to its firmware over Bluetooth.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <a class="button" href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/Et3BuD5c">Join the TestFlight beta</a>
                </p>
                <p class="muted small">
                    It is a beta, through Apple's TestFlight: install Apple's TestFlight app first, then open the link
                    on the iPhone, iPad or Mac. Source and issues: <a href={`${org}/apple`}>ternmesh/apple</a>.
                </p>
            </li>

            <li class="card" id="browser">
                <h2>In the browser</h2>
                <p class="muted">Chrome or Edge, on a computer or an Android phone.</p>
                <p>
                    Chats with contacts and groups, through a node plugged into the computer over USB, or one in
                    Bluetooth's reach. Nothing to install, and nothing runs on a server. Safari and Firefox cannot
                    reach a node yet.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <a class="button" href="/app">Open the app</a>
                    <a class="button secondary" href="/app?demo">Try it without a board</a>
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="muted small">
            What the apps send anywhere but to your node is on the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</Base>

<style>
    .apps {
        padding-top: 32px;
        padding-bottom: 48px;
        max-width: 44rem;
    }
    h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
        margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .lede {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    .list {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
        margin: 24px 0;
        display: grid;
        gap: 16px;
    }
    .note,
    .card {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 12px 16px;
    }
    .note {
        background: var(--accent-soft);
    }
    .card {
        background: var(--surface);
    }
    .card h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.3rem;
    }
    .card p {
        margin: 8px 0;
    }
    .card .muted:first-of-type {
        margin-top: 2px;
    }
    .small {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    a.button {
        display: inline-block;
        margin: 4px 8px 4px 0;
        padding: 9px 16px;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        border: 1px solid var(--accent);
        background: var(--accent);
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
    }
    a.button.secondary {
        background: transparent;
        color: var(--accent);
    }
</style>
